From 80a4dcfee2032b199ee797b0e0c45ffe8876415a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:43:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/22] Types: the type check (TypeScript 7.0.2, tsconfig.json,
 game/types, npm run typecheck)

TypeScript reads the JavaScript as it is (allowJs, noEmit) and checks only files that start with // @ts-check; none
does yet. game/types/game-data.d.ts is the game data's format (every section, with the phase 05 names),
save-data.d.ts the save (format 2, with trip), globals.d.ts what the classic scripts put on window (GAMEDATA,
PB_DATA, PB_VERSION, debugLog...). Strict null checks; a parameter without a JSDoc type is any for now.
TypeScript 7.0.2 (the native compiler, 2026-07-08) rather than 6.0.3: same results on this code, 4-7 times faster.
npm run format and format:check include the .d.ts files.
---
